\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. Come, let us to the Lord our God
\par With contrite hearts return;
\par Our God is gracious, nor will leave 
\par The desolate to mourn.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. His voice commands the tempest forth,
\par And stills the stormy wave;
\par And though His arm be strong to smite,
\par 'Tis also strong to save.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. Long hath the night of sorrow reigned;
\par The dawn shall bring us light;
\par God shall appear, and we shall rise
\par With gladness in His sight.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. Ourr hearts, if God we seek to know,
\par Shall know Him and rejoice;
\par His coming like the morn shall be,
\par Like morning songs His voice.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 5. As dew upon th tender herb,
\par Diffusing fragrance round;
\par As showers that usher in the spring,
\par And cheer the thirsty ground.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 6\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 6. So shall His presence bless our souls,
\par And shed a joyful light,
\par That hallowed morn shall chase away
\par The sorrows of the light.\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b 
\par }

